arrays, but the implementation is not straightforward because the arrays
have different numbers of (reported) beads.
For quantile normalization it will probably be necessary to pad the
arrays with smaller amounts of beads, where you would have to make a
decision on what the values should be in the padded data. (ie. Pad the
tails with the minimum and maximum values within the array, take a
sample from the existing data, or sort the data and take datapoints at
regular intervals)



